 variants_intro="Six different structures sit under the phrase business loan. Choosing the wrong one is what makes business credit feel expensive.",
 variants=[("Unsecured term loan","Fixed EMI, no collateral, assessed on ITR, GST returns and bank statements. Fast, and the default for amounts up to around ₹75 lakh.","brief"),
           ("Working capital / overdraft","A sanctioned limit you draw from as needed, with interest only on the utilised amount. The correct instrument for a seasonal or receivables-driven cycle.","coins"),
           ("Machinery &amp; equipment loan","Funds the asset and is secured by it. Longer tenure, lower rate, and often eligible for subsidy under state MSME schemes.","building"),
           ("Loan against property for business","The cheapest large-ticket business money available — your property backs a facility of ₹25 lakh to several crore at secured rates.","home"),
           ("MSME &amp; government schemes","Mudra, CGTMSE-backed collateral-free credit, Stand-Up India and state schemes. Paperwork-heavy, materially cheaper.","shield"),
           ("Invoice &amp; bill discounting","Convert approved invoices into cash immediately rather than waiting out the credit period. Priced on the buyer's credit, not only yours.","doc")],
